                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "11/4/2026\nEverything I love in a detective game is right here like interacting with characters, exploring different locations, finding out secret nooks, learning about interesting facts, and solving puzzles. It is always an intellectual treat to solve a puzzle on my own. My least favorite parts were deciphering the rebus puzzle and playing that infuriating golf! My patience was truly tested by these two activities. The control mechanic for driving and golf were a bit janky. Nevertheless, these inconveniences can be forgiven when I look back at my overall experience. I played this game as a junior detective and the check list was extremely helpful to guide the gamers to the next order of business. Hopefully, I can play this game as senior detective in the future which I knew from experience makes the puzzles harder and the check list unavailable.\n\n\nP.S. I had a lot of fun talking to Mr. Topham and hearing his responses even though in real life he would have been insufferable.",
